{"author":"RebarBotNava","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","author_sig":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","data":{"body":"Phase 2 complete — fix pushed to Gerrit change 2360.\n\n## Root cause (proven, Phase 1)\nThe op-cert signing subsystem had NO guard surfacing a signing key whose public\ncounterpart the same-environment verify path cannot resolve. `mint_opcert_record`\n(_opcert_signing.py) never consulted `_opcert_own_public_keys` (its sole caller was\nthe verify path, :550), and no counterpart check existed in mcp_server.py /\n_mcp_health.py / _opcert_binding.py. This is the exact divergence class Gerrit 2337\n(parent d26a) fixed — write-side key resolution diverging from verify-side resolution\nso signing succeeds but verify returns `foreign_key` and the claim gate refuses every\nticket — with nothing to surface it. Genuine omission.\n\n## Classification & legitimacy\n`incomplete-implementation` (NOT feature-request): parent d26a-8ffa-97cd-4b2a\n(dire-expectable-terrapin, closed plan_defect) explicitly SPLIT its deferred AC5\n(mint-time warning) + AC6 (startup health check) into THIS ticket as \"additive guards\nagainst the class regressing.\" Design authority cited → completing/wiring the approved\nwork is restoration, not creation.\n\n## Fix (per the operator's reframed AC3)\nTwo additive, NON-REFUSING guards:\n- AC1/AC2 (mint warning): `_warn_if_verify_cannot_resolve` in `mint_opcert_record`\n  logs a WARNING naming key_path + principal when the same-env verify resolver cannot\n  resolve a public counterpart for the key just signed under; still returns the\n  signature. Silent on the healthy path.\n- AC3 (serve-degraded, NEVER abort): `opcert_signing_status` /\n  `opcert_signer_degraded` / `run_startup_opcert_check` in `_mcp_health.py` check the\n  ONE non-redundant condition the derived-key path can't catch: does the bound signer's\n  public key match the pinned `rebar.attest.trusted_env` key for its principal. Exposed\n  as a `/health` \"opcert\" field + a boot warning. `expected` gates strictness like\n  `store_status` (only when `.rebar/trusted_environments.yaml` is present), because\n  required-env binding is advisory today (ADR 0104 dec. 3). Did NOT extend\n  `compose_startup_opcert_binding` to abort; did NOT add a redundant derive probe.\n\n## Test (RED->GREEN, held-out, mutation-checked)\n`tests/unit/test_opcert_public_counterpart_guard_879b.py` (7 tests). Seen RED first\n(AC1 on assertion `[]`; AC3 on AttributeError = capability absent), GREEN after.\nMutation check (sandboxed, sandbox-exec): removing the mint guard -> AC1 RED; forcing\n`opcert_signer_degraded` False -> both AC3 degraded tests RED; restored -> GREEN. Tests\nassert observable output (log messages / dict fields), not private names.\n\n## Scope & safety\n- Caller sweep: production explicit-signer paths run inside `bound_signer(signer)`\n  (jobs.py:91), so the mint guard's resolver won't false-warn. All production\n  environment self-signing funnels through the guarded `mint_opcert_record`.\n- Restoration not creation (cited design authority d26a); no new dependency (all\n  imports pre-existing); no pre-existing test weakened.\n- Regression sweep: 349 passed / 3 skipped across opcert/mcp_health/trusted_env/signing.\n  Lint + typecheck clean. Non-test diff 109 lines (< 150 floor -> no review-plan needed).\n\n## Siblings (Step 7)\n- Axis 1 (construct): the only environment-derivation mint path is `mint_opcert_record`\n  -- covered. No other instances.\n- Axis 2 (parity): `sign_opcert_manifest` (:611) signs an op-cert bypassing the guard,\n  but it takes an EXPLICIT caller-supplied key and has NO production caller (test/remote-\n  cert primitive, keystone e4df) used to sign under deliberately foreign/remote keys.\n  879b's env-derivation divergence cannot arise there, and the same-env warning would\n  false-positive on foreign-key signing -> N/A by design, not MISSING. `/health` is the\n  single health surface; status stashed for both http + stdio.\n\n## Defect origin\nAttributed by scope-of-work to d26a-8ffa-97cd-4b2a (the parent that scoped AC5/AC6 and\ndeferred them into this ticket). Omission -> no introducing commit; will be recorded via\nthe non-gated `--caused-by=d26a-8ffa-97cd-4b2a` on close. `caused_by` link already\nrecorded in Phase 1.\n\n## Replication\nOriginal report (\"no guard surfaces a signing key with no usable public cert\") no longer\nholds: the mint path warns, and `/health` reports a degraded `opcert` field + boot\nwarning on the pinned-key mismatch.\n\n## Gerrit\nChange 2360 — https://rebar.solutions.navateam.com/c/rebar/+/2360 — awaiting\nLLM-Review +1 AND Verified +1 before Submit."},"env_id":"b8a354e0-12c3-4cf2-bbf1-fcc9685d5126","event_type":"COMMENT","timestamp":1787966102263938001,"uuid":"39847453-9231-416f-872c-f8e59f7b5f0d"}